===Etymology 1===
From Proto-Finnic ''*kurki'', from {{etyl|urj-pro|fi}} {{m|urj-pro|*karke}}, itself an onomatopoeic word. Cognates include Estonian {{m|et|kurg}} and Northern Sami {{m|se|guorga}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|lang=fi|[ˈkurki]}}
* {{rhymes|lang=fi|urki}}
* {{hyphenation|kur|ki|lang=fi}}

====Noun====
{{fi-noun}}

# [[crane]], ''Grus grus'' {{gloss|large wading bird}}
# Any bird of the family [[Gruidae]], the cranes.

